{:edb/db-before-t 1718 :edb/db-after-t 1719 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535031 50 #inst "2026-10-08T15:14:34.581Z" 13194139535031 true] [17592186064254 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327800 13194139535031 true] [17592186068847 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327814 13194139535031 true] [17592186083110 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327819 13194139535031 true] [17592186083240 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327803 13194139535031 true] [17592186096541 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327806 13194139535031 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327822 13194139535031 true] [17592186105635 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327809 13194139535031 true] [17592186327800 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327801 13194139535031 true] [17592186327800 1089 "q-128332" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327800 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535031 true] [17592186327800 1100 "Consider the function $f$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nCalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{-7(4x-5)}{(2x^2-5x-3)^2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe slope of the tangent line to the graph of $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." 13194139535031 true] [17592186327800 1113 #uuid "2bfbd25a-1326-5d7c-9e85-767cc1198974" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327800 1145 "The slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(2).$ In part 1, we found\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{7(5-4x)}{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=2,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{7(5-4\\cdot 2)}{(2\\cdot {2}^{2}-5\\cdot 2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot (-3)}{(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve at $x=2$ is $-\\frac{21}{25}.$" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327802 13194139535031 true] [17592186327801 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535031 true] [17592186327801 1041 "field-1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327801 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327802 13194139535031 true] [17592186327801 1110 #uuid "b8be7543-a7cf-5018-8b39-c018360a6399" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327802 1034 "-\\frac{21}{25}" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535031 true] [17592186327802 1111 #uuid "f66003b7-cfcc-5de3-93c9-63ff780a4390" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327803 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327804 13194139535031 true] [17592186327803 1089 "q-128333" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327803 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535031 true] [17592186327803 1100 "Consider the function $f$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nCalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{-7(4x-5)}{(2x^2-5x-3)^2}$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe slope of the tangent line to the graph of $y=f(x)$ at $x=2$ is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{21}{25}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nConsider a function $g(x)$ such that $g(2)=-2$ and ${g}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ If $h(x)=\\frac{5-25f(x)}{g(x)+3},$ then ${h}^{′}(2)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\nAt which values of $x\\in (-\\frac{1}{2},3)$ does $f$ have a critical point?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The function $f$ has a critical point at $x=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." 13194139535031 true] [17592186327803 1113 #uuid "33f175dd-a9d4-5d3d-aba6-42b4e89e487b" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327803 1145 "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nIn part 1, we obtained\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{7(5-4x)}{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n* First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7(5-4x)}{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)^{2}} & =0 \\\\ 7(5-4x) & =0 \\\\ 5-4x & =0 \\\\ 4x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$\n\n* Second, we find the points in the domain of $f(x)$ where ${f}^{′}(x)$ does not exist. Factoring our expression for ${f}^{′}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{7(5-4x)}{[(2x+1)(x-3)]^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ does not exist at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=3.$ But these points do not lie in the interval $(-\\frac{1}{2},3).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the only critical point of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327805 13194139535031 true] [17592186327804 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535031 true] [17592186327804 1041 "field-1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327804 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327805 13194139535031 true] [17592186327804 1110 #uuid "91e0990c-db75-5693-9748-4087db6ca9ad" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327805 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327805 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535031 true] [17592186327805 1111 #uuid "fc2bc84d-e21c-5d61-b478-270c07edb55d" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327806 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327807 13194139535031 true] [17592186327806 1089 "q-128335" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327806 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535031 true] [17592186327806 1100 "Consider the function $f$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nCalculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{′}(x)\\,=\\,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327806 1113 #uuid "0bb8566e-0896-530f-9a63-4498d25abe00" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327806 1145 "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=7$ and $v(x)=2{x}^{2}-5x-3,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=0,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=4x-5.\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x){v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0)\\cdot (2{x}^{2}-5x-3)-7\\cdot (4x-5)}{{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-7\\cdot (4x-5)}{{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(5-4x)}{{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327807 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327808 1319