              \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(x)$ has \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ local maxima and \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ local minima." 13194139535031 true] [17592186327809 1113 #uuid "4346e073-2d30-5ade-a6c2-25bdeeed7387" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327809 1145 "We have the derivative \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{7(4x-5)}{(2{x}^{2}-5x-3)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the critical point $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$ We use the first derivative test to determine whether this point is a local maximum or minimum.\n\nLet's choose the test points $x=0,2$ and evaluate the first derivative at these points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{7(4\\cdot 0-5)}{(2\\cdot {0}^{2}-5\\cdot 0-3)^{2}}=\\frac{35}{9}>0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{7(4\\cdot 2-5)}{(2\\cdot {2}^{2}-5\\cdot 2-3)^{2}}=-\\frac{21}{25}<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe summarize the information in the table shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{4})$ | $\\frac{5}{4}$ | $(\\frac{5}{4},3)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $0$ |  | $2$ |\n| ${f}^{′}$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\n \nFinally, let's use the table above to classify the critical point.\n\n* At $x=\\frac{5}{4},$ the first derivative changes sign from positive to negative. Therefore, $x=\\frac{5}{4}$ is a local maximum.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(x)$ has $1$ local maximum and $0$ local minima on the interval $x\\in (-\\frac{1}{2},3).$" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327810 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327811 13194139535031 true] [17592186327810 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535031 true] [17592186327810 1041 "field-1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327810 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327811 13194139535031 true] [17592186327810 1110 #uuid "4033eb5f-f2d3-516f-b7a9-a05c641158a1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327811 1034 "1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327811 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535031 true] [17592186327811 1111 #uuid "93aaceda-b6ab-531e-8d49-1d20aa189f6e" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327812 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327813 13194139535031 true] [17592186327812 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535031 true] [17592186327812 1041 "field-2" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327812 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327813 13194139535031 true] [17592186327812 1110 #uuid "852e1644-4343-5c83-9c3f-d540af58cfd7" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327813 1034 "0" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327813 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535031 true] [17592186327813 1111 #uuid "f5ddb6cd-9e1b-5f1e-a24a-c2c1f0e45f35" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327815 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327817 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1089 "q-128339" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1100 "Consider the function $f$ defined by $f(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}.$\n\nEarlier