            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1113 #uuid "5f5dc83b-4d6f-5a90-9b27-05db05e5bf2b" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327814 1145 "First, we factor the numerator and denominator of $f(x)$:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{7}{2{x}^{2}-5x-3}=\\frac{7}{(x-3)(2x+1)}\n$$\n\nOur task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x-3}+\\frac{B}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(2x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n7=A(2x+1)+B(x-3).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1)+B(-\\frac{1}{2}-3) \\\\ 7 & =-\\frac{7}{2}B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7 & =A(2\\cdot 3+1)+B(3-3) \\\\ 7 & =7A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{(x-3)(2x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{2}{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }(\\frac{1}{x-3}-\\frac{2}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x-3}-2{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $A=1$ and $B=-2.$" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327815 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327816 13194139535031 true] [17592186327815 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535031 true] [17592186327815 1041 "field-1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327815 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327816 13194139535031 true] [17592186327815 1110 #uuid "83fdb9a8-8f9d-5b98-bf33-701f4df683f5" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327816 1034 "1" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327816 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535031 true] [17592186327816 1111 #uuid "d01d4f0d-5a05-513a-9e4f-ec33484a4d10" 13194139535031 true] [17592186327817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327818 13194139535031 true] [17592186327817 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535031 true] [17592186327817 1041 "field-2" 13194139535031 true] [175921863