                              \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $f(x)$ has \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ local maxima and \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,$ local minima.\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nGiven that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=A{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x-3}+B{\\int }_{4}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}x}{2x+1}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are constants, find $A$ and $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $A=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $1$                \n                  